#: ../../source/release-process.rst:4 17a339e706284f4a85c691897df85738
msgid "Release process"
msgstr "Processus de publication"

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:6 aefbb5a49b9341f68f5086531f4363de
msgid ""
"This page describes how a Maigret release is cut, what each git tag in "
"the repository means, and which automation reacts to what. It is written "
"for maintainers and for downstream packagers who need to know which ref "
"to build from."
msgstr ""
"Cette page décrit comment une version de Maigret est publiée, ce que "
"signifie chaque tag git du dépôt et quelle automatisation réagit à quoi. "
"Elle s'adresse aux mainteneurs et aux empaqueteurs en aval, qui doivent "
"savoir depuis quelle référence construire."

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:12 1e74bb38a83f4bf2bcb877afebcf6256
msgid "Where the version lives"
msgstr "Où se trouve le numéro de version"

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:14 b6576061e660449893640bc12d1697e5
msgid "The version is stored in two files and both have to be changed together:"
msgstr ""
"La version est stockée dans deux fichiers, qui doivent être modifiés "
"ensemble :"

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:16 bdc5ce0a756048588fc6bd4fc5babe57
msgid "``pyproject.toml``, the ``version`` field under ``[tool.poetry]``"
msgstr "``pyproject.toml``, le champ ``version`` sous ``[tool.poetry]``"

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:17 cef162954f8e4b84bc1a036aba630ad8
msgid "``maigret/__version__.py``, the ``__version__`` string"
msgstr "``maigret/__version__.py``, la chaîne ``__version__``"

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:19 237e5c1ed8cf4a2a9b443fe1f4b1281e
msgid ""
"``maigret/__version__.py`` is what the snap packaging reads through "
"``craftctl set version``, and ``pyproject.toml`` is what ends up in the "
"PyPI metadata. A mismatch between them produces a package that reports "
"one version and is published as another."
msgstr ""
"``maigret/__version__.py`` est ce que lit l'empaquetage snap via "
"``craftctl set version``, et ``pyproject.toml`` est ce qui se retrouve "
"dans les métadonnées PyPI. Une divergence entre les deux produit un "
"paquet qui annonce une version et qui est publié sous une autre."

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:25 a92d26566ec94a2f940411d2aaf8dbf4
msgid "Cutting a release"
msgstr "Préparer une version"

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:27 f34e7a60d13d4d379930f58cee1bf22b
msgid ""
"Branch off ``main``. The branch is normally named after the version, for "
"example ``0.6.5``."
msgstr ""
"Créez une branche à partir de ``main``. Elle porte normalement le nom de "
"la version, par exemple ``0.6.5``."

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:29 025928a1d2054936a551727ac52e5a34
msgid "Bump the two version files on that branch."
msgstr "Incrémentez les deux fichiers de version sur cette branche."

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:30 b576ce4c678a4c62ae94596beba1db7c
msgid ""
"Open a pull request for the bump, so the change is reviewed like any "
"other."
msgstr ""
"Ouvrez une pull request pour cette montée de version, afin qu'elle soit "
"relue comme n'importe quel autre changement."

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:32 ad1c5257714046a1b132082636dcbd73
msgid ""
"The release branch is where the tag will live. It is deliberately "
"separate from ``main``: the tag has to point at a commit whose version "
"files already say the new number, and ``main`` only receives that commit "
"after the release is out."
msgstr ""
"C'est sur la branche de version que vivra le tag. Elle est volontairement"
" distincte de ``main`` : le tag doit pointer sur un commit dont les "
"fichiers de version annoncent déjà le nouveau numéro, et ``main`` ne "
"reçoit ce commit qu'une fois la version publiée."

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:37 9b0fd23d4f83496aa2b3b0339aa9b63b
msgid "Publishing"
msgstr "Publication"

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:39 cd1ba051900c45f68ad00bc86f881d50
msgid ""
"Create a GitHub Release whose tag is ``vX.Y.Z`` and whose target is the "
"release branch. Publishing it is the event that starts everything else, "
"so the release notes should be finished before you publish rather than "
"after."
msgstr ""
"Créez une GitHub Release dont le tag est ``vX.Y.Z`` et dont la cible est "
"la branche de version. C'est sa publication qui déclenche tout le reste, "
"donc les notes de version doivent être terminées avant de publier, pas "
"après."

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:43 564a58b206c14bc8a6ad3b7404fa9fff
msgid "Two workflows listen for ``release: types: [published]``:"
msgstr "Deux workflows écoutent ``release: types: [published]`` :"

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:45 ea4d208e7f084977a98696fbff688f94
msgid ""
"``python-publish.yml`` builds the source distribution and the wheel and "
"uploads them to PyPI through trusted publishing."
msgstr ""
"``python-publish.yml`` construit la distribution source et la wheel, puis"
" les téléverse sur PyPI via le trusted publishing."

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:47 af70ac77d9864f228f7ca81e486f3876
msgid ""
"``pyinstaller.yml`` builds ``maigret_standalone.exe`` under Wine and "
"attaches it to the release. The binary appears a few minutes after the "
"release itself, because PyInstaller is slow under Wine."
msgstr ""
"``pyinstaller.yml`` construit ``maigret_standalone.exe`` sous Wine et "
"l'attache à la release. Le binaire apparaît quelques minutes après la "
"release elle-même, car PyInstaller est lent sous Wine."

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:51 dcbf2f54af9d498d9ab76133fe766e0f
msgid ""
"Both check out ``refs/tags/vX.Y.Z``, so both build the released code "
"rather than the current head of a branch."
msgstr ""
"Les deux font un checkout de ``refs/tags/vX.Y.Z`` : ils construisent donc"
" le code publié, et non la tête actuelle d'une branche."

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:55 795f5e6ef9c54986aafe1e91e65752e7
msgid ""
"The ``pypi`` environment has no protection rules, so publishing any "
"release sends a package straight to PyPI with no human gate. Publishing a"
" test release from a branch whose version is not yet on PyPI will publish"
" that version for real."
msgstr ""
"L'environnement ``pypi`` n'a aucune règle de protection : publier une "
"release quelconque envoie le paquet directement sur PyPI, sans validation"
" humaine. Publier une release de test depuis une branche dont la version "
"n'est pas encore sur PyPI publiera cette version pour de bon."

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:61 5ddb2c3d69154ecbb85d3409d3322111
msgid "After the release"
msgstr "Après la publication"

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:63 517ac4e667aa440c80cd998100432260
msgid ""
"Merge the release branch into ``main``. In practice this happens a couple"
" of minutes after the release is published."
msgstr ""
"Fusionnez la branche de version dans ``main``. En pratique, cela se fait "
"quelques minutes après la publication."

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:66 07b11fd6ec564244a88153832522526f
msgid ""
"The push to ``main`` is a separate trigger and starts the routine "
"automation: the nightly Windows build, the Docker Hub images, the site "
"database refresh and the test suite."
msgstr ""
"Le push sur ``main`` est un déclencheur distinct, qui lance "
"l'automatisation de routine : la construction nocturne pour Windows, les "
"images Docker Hub, le rafraîchissement de la base de sites et la suite de"
" tests."

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:70 daa606217c2a4fad89b8dc9a1cbe017f
msgid ""
"Because the release branch is merged with a squash, the commit that lands"
" on ``main`` is not the commit the tag points at. This means ``vX.Y.Z`` "
"is not an ancestor of ``main``. It is expected, and it is why a packager "
"should build from the tag rather than looking for it in the branch "
"history."
msgstr ""
"Comme la branche de version est fusionnée en squash, le commit qui arrive"
" sur ``main`` n'est pas celui sur lequel pointe le tag. Autrement dit, "
"``vX.Y.Z`` n'est pas un ancêtre de ``main``. C'est attendu, et c'est la "
"raison pour laquelle un empaqueteur doit construire depuis le tag plutôt "
"que de le chercher dans l'historique de la branche."

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:76 1fc5ebf8ebde4634917f70b5e6a06681
msgid "Tags in this repository"
msgstr "Les tags de ce dépôt"

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:78 b3d0729bb2b2432fac9969ed9600c617
msgid ""
"**Release tags**, ``vX.Y.Z``. Immutable, one per release, pointing at the"
" tip of a release branch. These are the only tags a packager should build"
" from."
msgstr ""
"**Tags de version**, ``vX.Y.Z``. Immuables, un par version, pointant sur "
"la tête d'une branche de version. Ce sont les seuls tags depuis lesquels "
"un empaqueteur doit construire."

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:81 6328e93333ab4c8e8204cf15a6f9b3f0
msgid ""
"**Nightly tags**, ``nightly-main`` and ``nightly-dev``. Moving tags. "
"Every push to the matching branch rebuilds the Windows binary and force-"
"updates the tag to the built commit, so the tag always matches the "
"attached ``.exe``. The releases behind them are marked as prereleases so "
"they never take the \"latest\" marker from a real release. Never pin "
"anything to these: the ref is stable but its content is not."
msgstr ""
"**Tags nocturnes**, ``nightly-main`` et ``nightly-dev``. Des tags "
"mobiles. Chaque push sur la branche correspondante reconstruit le binaire"
" Windows et force la mise à jour du tag vers le commit construit, de "
"sorte que le tag corresponde toujours au ``.exe`` attaché. Les releases "
"associées sont marquées comme préversions, afin de ne jamais prendre le "
"marqueur « latest » d'une vraie version. N'épinglez jamais quoi que ce "
"soit dessus : la référence est stable, mais son contenu ne l'est pas."

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:88 7403364086e84a208f960ad875e398b6
msgid ""
"**Legacy tags**, ``main``, ``dev``, ``test`` and ``dev-564`` through "
"``dev-571``. Left over from an earlier version of the Windows build, "
"which used the branch name directly as the tag name. Nothing creates or "
"updates them any more. Two of them still carry GitHub releases with a "
"Windows binary attached, built in April 2026, so anything downloaded from"
" them is old."
msgstr ""
"**Tags hérités**, ``main``, ``dev``, ``test`` et ``dev-564`` à "
"``dev-571``. Reliquats d'une ancienne version de la construction Windows,"
" qui utilisait directement le nom de la branche comme nom de tag. Plus "
"rien ne les crée ni ne les met à jour. Deux d'entre eux portent encore "
"des releases GitHub avec un binaire Windows attaché, construit en avril "
"2026 : tout ce qui en est téléchargé est donc ancien."

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:95 499996b2bb6e49f2841c32bb58528637
msgid ""
"A tag named ``main`` shadows the branch of the same name. ``git rev-parse"
" main`` warns that the refname is ambiguous and answers with the tag, so "
"``git show main:some/file`` reads from the tag's commit and not from the "
"branch head. Tools that resolve a bare ref hit this too: a remote build "
"that is told to build ``main`` may build the tag. Use ``refs/heads/main``"
" explicitly, or clone with ``--no-tags``. The site data workflow works "
"around it with a ``git tag -d main`` step before it touches any ref."
msgstr ""
"Un tag nommé ``main`` masque la branche du même nom. ``git rev-parse "
"main`` avertit que la référence est ambiguë et répond avec le tag, si "
"bien que ``git show main:un/fichier`` lit le commit du tag et non la tête"
" de la branche. Les outils qui résolvent une référence nue tombent dans "
"le même piège : une construction distante à laquelle on demande ``main`` "
"risque de construire le tag. Utilisez explicitement ``refs/heads/main``, "
"ou clonez avec ``--no-tags``. Le workflow des données de sites contourne "
"le problème avec une étape ``git tag -d main`` avant de toucher à la "
"moindre référence."

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:104 24e401ea5e3c47e686b40255ab6cedaf
msgid "Where the artifacts end up"
msgstr "Où atterrissent les artefacts"

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:106 181b3e7dbf0f41799e28eb956e8f3e66
msgid "Published automatically on release:"
msgstr "Publiés automatiquement à chaque release :"

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:108 ad0c797d160441e199fecf92ff51f677
msgid "**PyPI**, the source distribution and the wheel."
msgstr "**PyPI**, la distribution source et la wheel."

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:109 f83b2aa49f584014ab6a2516b60ce11b
msgid "**GitHub release assets**, the Windows ``maigret_standalone.exe``."
msgstr ""
"**Les assets de la release GitHub**, le ``maigret_standalone.exe`` pour "
"Windows."

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:111 27c81092af374faa8a7bdd3eec745e1b
msgid "Published automatically on every push to ``main``:"
msgstr "Publiés automatiquement à chaque push sur ``main`` :"

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:113 b4f0d324b8794cf4a27fc500fa138912
msgid "**Docker Hub**, the CLI and web images."
msgstr "**Docker Hub**, les images CLI et web."

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:115 d7a8efffcb2844a0b8eed26caf6da766
msgid "Published by hand:"
msgstr "Publiés à la main :"

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:117 e45ef970948044078020146a411921ee
msgid ""
"**Snap**, built with ``snapcraft`` and uploaded to the ``latest/stable`` "
"channel for amd64 and arm64. Uploading a revision does not touch the "
"store listing: the summary, the description and the icon change only when"
" ``snapcraft upload-metadata <snap-file>`` is run, so run it whenever "
"those fields change in ``snap/snapcraft.yaml``, or the store keeps "
"serving the old text."
msgstr ""
"**Snap**, construit avec ``snapcraft`` et téléversé sur le canal "
"``latest/stable`` pour amd64 et arm64. Téléverser une révision ne touche "
"pas à la fiche du store : le résumé, la description et l'icône ne "
"changent que lorsque ``snapcraft upload-metadata <fichier-snap>`` est "
"exécuté. Lancez-le donc dès que ces champs changent dans "
"``snap/snapcraft.yaml``, sinon le store continue de servir l'ancien "
"texte."

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:124 edcc5592473f4eb5bbf9f9fab4d50848
msgid "Maintained downstream, outside this repository:"
msgstr "Maintenus en aval, en dehors de ce dépôt :"

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:126 da25d33954774695b15ca4ea695982ba
msgid ""
"The AUR, Homebrew core, MacPorts and nixpkgs normally follow a new "
"release within a day or two without being asked."
msgstr ""
"AUR, Homebrew core, MacPorts et nixpkgs suivent normalement une nouvelle "
"version en un jour ou deux, sans qu'on ait à le demander."

#: ../../source/release-process.rst:128 edbbf6cb578d4be9acbbfb2d7a000193
msgid "BlackArch is updated through a pull request to the BlackArch repository."
msgstr "BlackArch est mis à jour via une pull request sur le dépôt BlackArch."

